- Q' is the twisted-constant Z_p-sheaf attached to the étale quotient, with F an isomorphism;
- P' is attached to the dual of the multiplicative part, with F = p·(iso).
M also carries an integrable connection ∇ respecting the extension, and a horizontal Frobenius F_M: F_S^*M → M inducing these maps on graded pieces. Over S_0 one adds a splitting 'Fil' of M_0 compatible with F_{M_0}; this is the Hodge filtration, which for ordinary groups is a complement to the étale part. The page asks whether D: BTO(S_0)^op → C is an equivalence. This is a Dieudonné-theoretic classification of ordinary BT groups over a smooth base via Frobenius-crystal data in the style of Katz/Deligne–Illusie, with explicit unit-root/slope pieces.
